      "question": "My manager wants a quick look at the oil condition on Transformer 1 at site MAIN. From the latest reading and the stats over the full available window, give me dielectric_rigidity, interfacial_v, oxygen, nitrogen and dbds, and say whether any of them moved in a direction that points to moisture ingress, air ingress or oil ageing. Rank the three concerns from most to least supported by the data. Don't use the combustible gases for this. If dielectric_rigidity or interfacial_v has no data, say so and base the ranking on oxygen and nitrogen only.",
      "answer": "**Transformer 1 \u2014 MAIN:** Full window: **15\u201319 January 2024**, five readings each, no missing data. Latest: **19 January 2024**\u2014historical, not current. Units were not supplied.\n\n| Measurement | Latest | Mean | Min\u2013max | Std. dev. | First \u2192 latest |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| dielectric_rigidity | 55 | 54.6 | 53\u201356 | 1.02 | 55 \u2192 55 |\n| interfacial_v | 45 | 45.0 | 44\u201346 | 0.63 | 45 \u2192 45 |\n| oxygen | 5,850 | 5,822 | 5,700\u20135,900 | 68.82 | 5,860 \u2192 5,850 |\n| nitrogen | 27,850 | 27,868.4 | 27,700\u201328,000 | 103.32 | 27,842 \u2192 27,850 |\n| dbds | 19 | 19.0 | 18\u201320 | 0.63 | 19 \u2192 19 |\n\n**Concern ranking:** The data do **not support a meaningful separation**; all three are weak/unsupported:\n1. **Air ingress:** At most a negligible hint from nitrogen (+8); oxygen decreased (\u221210), with no sustained joint rise.\n2. **Moisture ingress \u2014 tied with oil ageing:** Dielectric rigidity briefly fell to 53 but recovered to 55; no sustained deterioration.\n3. **Oil ageing \u2014 tied with moisture ingress:** Interfacial tension briefly fell to 44 but recovered to 45. DBDS stayed unchanged overall and is principally a corrosive-sulfur indicator, not proof of ageing.\n\n**Bottom line:** Small fluctuations, no sustained adverse direction. No combustible gases used.",
      "score": {
        "scorer": "llm_judge",
        "passed": true,
        "score": 1.0,
